title: Privacy Policy
description: How Naked Tech collects, uses, stores and discloses personal information, including contact forms, service records, analytics and advertising choices.
---

<header class="bg-inverse pb-16 pt-32 text-inverse-ink md:pb-20 md:pt-40">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 text-center">
        <p class="mb-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Effective 1 September 2026</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight md:text-6xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-inverse-ink/75 md:text-xl">
            What Naked Tech collects, why we need it and the choices you have.
        </p>
    </div>
</header>

<div class="bg-canvas py-16 md:py-24">
    <article class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
        <div class="space-y-10 rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-8 text-ink shadow-sm md:p-12">
            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-operator">
                <h2 id="privacy-operator" class="text-2xl font-bold">1. Who is responsible</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Naked Tech is operated by Peter Reginald, ABN 57 221 340 918, a sole trader trading as Digital Sanctum and Naked Tech (“Naked Tech”, “we”, “us” or “our”). This policy applies to personal information handled through nakedtech.au, enquiries, bookings, service delivery, invoices and related communications.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collection">
                <h2 id="privacy-collection" class="text-2xl font-bold">2. Information we collect</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">Depending on how you deal with us, we may collect:</p>
                <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-muted">
                    <li>your name, email address, phone number and service address;</li>
                    <li>your enquiry, the technology problem you describe and your communication preferences;</li>
                    <li>booking, quote, invoice, payment-status and transaction records;</li>
                    <li>concise service notes about the agreed work, devices, products and outcomes;</li>
                    <li>correspondence, feedback, access or correction requests, and complaints;</li>
                    <li>website request information such as IP address, date and time, requested page, browser and device information used for delivery, reliability and security; and</li>
                    <li>if you enable optional tracking, the analytics or advertising information described below.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Please do not send passwords, authentication codes, recovery material, banking PINs, card security codes, government identifiers or other sensitive information through an enquiry form. During a service, you enter credentials yourself. We do not record, photograph, copy, transmit or retain them.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-collection-methods">
                <h2 id="privacy-collection-methods" class="text-2xl font-bold">3. How we collect information</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    We usually collect information directly from you when you use the contact form, call, email, request or accept a quote, book a service, receive a service, pay an invoice or make a privacy request. Website infrastructure also receives ordinary technical request information when your browser connects. If another person makes an enquiry for you, we may receive your details from that person and will use them only where it is reasonable to do so.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    You can browse the public website without telling us your name. You may use a preferred name for a preliminary enquiry, but we may need accurate contact, address and billing details before confirming or delivering a service. If you do not provide enough information, we may be unable to respond, assess suitability, confirm a booking or provide the requested service.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-purposes">
                <h2 id="privacy-purposes" class="text-2xl font-bold">4. Why we use information</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">We use personal information where reasonably necessary to:</p>
                <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-muted">
                    <li>respond to enquiries and assess whether a service is suitable;</li>
                    <li>quote, schedule, provide and follow up agreed services;</li>
                    <li>communicate about appointments, safety, products and service outcomes;</li>
                    <li>issue invoices, record payments and meet tax, accounting and other legal obligations;</li>
                    <li>handle feedback, disputes, consumer-law matters and privacy requests;</li>
                    <li>protect customers, systems and the business from misuse, fraud and security threats; and</li>
                    <li>measure website use or advertising campaigns when you have enabled the relevant optional tracking category.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Submitting a service enquiry is not a subscription to unrelated email or SMS marketing. If we offer optional marketing in future, we will use an appropriate consent and unsubscribe process.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-form">
                <h2 id="privacy-form" class="text-2xl font-bold">5. Contact form and browser storage</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    The embedded contact form is delivered from forms.digitalsanctum.com.au through Digital Sanctum’s Sanctum Forms system. It asks for your name, email address and message, with a phone number optional. To help us understand the enquiry, the Naked Tech page may also pass the page path, relevant service category and the campaign parameters <code class="rounded bg-surface-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">utm_source</code>, <code class="rounded bg-surface-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">utm_medium</code>, <code class="rounded bg-surface-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">utm_campaign</code> and <code class="rounded bg-surface-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">utm_content</code> when present. It does not pass other URL parameters.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    As you type, the form saves an unfinished draft in local storage for the forms.digitalsanctum.com.au site in that browser. A successfully submitted draft is cleared. If you do not submit it, the draft remains until you or your browser clears that site’s stored data. The form also stores its colour-theme choice locally.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Naked Tech separately stores your colour-theme choice and a record of your tracking preferences on nakedtech.au. The tracking record is necessary to remember an acceptance or rejection; rejecting optional tracking does not itself load Google Analytics or Meta Pixel.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    To protect the enquiry form from automated misuse, Sanctum Forms may compare keyed pseudonyms derived from selected identity fields and the request network address with recent submissions. The security evidence does not contain the raw identity values or raw network address, is kept separately from optional tracking, and is scheduled for deletion after 30 days. A suspicious submission may be held in quarantine and will not trigger an owner notification, lead webhook or advertising-conversion event.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    When the risk rule requires additional verification, the form loads Cloudflare Turnstile. Cloudflare may process security signals such as IP address, TLS fingerprint, browser user-agent, site key and form origin to distinguish people from bots; Naked Tech does not send Cloudflare the words, email address, phone number or other answers entered in the form. Turnstile is a necessary security control rather than Analytics or Advertising, so it may run even when optional tracking is rejected. See Cloudflare’s <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-bold text-accent-ink underline hover:text-ink">Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-tracking">
                <h2 id="privacy-tracking" class="text-2xl font-bold">6. Optional analytics and advertising</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Analytics and advertising tracking are off until you select the relevant category. The choices are separate and neither checkbox is preselected.
                </p>
                <div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto">
                    <table class="w-full min-w-[36rem] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
                        <thead>
                            <tr class="border-b-2 border-ink">
                                <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-bold">Category</th>
                                <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-bold">Provider and information</th>
                                <th class="py-3 font-bold">Purpose</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody class="text-muted">
                            <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                                <th class="py-4 pr-4 font-bold text-ink">Analytics</th>
                                <td class="py-4 pr-4">Google Analytics 4 may receive page and interaction events, campaign information, predefined search-demand categories, approximate location derived from IP address, and browser or device information. It may set or read analytics cookies and similar identifiers.</td>
                                <td class="py-4">Understand visits, service-page use, privacy-safe service selection, unmet service demand, referral interest, phone-link activations and successful enquiries so we can improve the site and service offering.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr class="border-b border-line align-top">
                                <th class="py-4 pr-4 font-bold text-ink">Advertising</th>
                                <td class="py-4 pr-4">Meta Pixel may receive page views, service-view, phone-contact and successful-enquiry events, campaign information, IP address, and browser, device, cookie or similar identifier information.</td>
                                <td class="py-4">Measure advertising performance and understand which campaigns lead to enquiries.</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    We do not intentionally send Google or Meta the text you enter in the contact form, your email address, phone number or service address through these website events. Their own handling is described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-bold text-accent-ink underline hover:text-ink">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-bold text-accent-ink underline hover:text-ink">Meta Privacy Policy</a>.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Site-search words stay in your browser and are not sent to Naked Tech, Google or Meta. If Analytics is already enabled, Google Analytics may receive only a predefined service or referral category, the result state, the search entry point, the current page path, an allowlisted internal service destination and whether you expressed service or referral interest. It never receives the words you typed, and a search made before consent is not queued for later reporting.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    You can accept, reject or change these categories at any time using <button type="button" class="font-bold text-accent-ink underline hover:text-ink" data-tracking-preferences-open>Tracking preferences</button>. Turning off an active category reloads the page and prevents that provider from loading on later pages. It does not recall information already sent to the provider; you can also clear existing cookies and site data in your browser.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-disclosure">
                <h2 id="privacy-disclosure" class="text-2xl font-bold">7. When we disclose information</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    We do not sell or rent customer lists. We may disclose only the information reasonably needed to service providers that help us host the website and forms, protect the form through Cloudflare Turnstile, operate business email and storage, issue invoices, process a payment method you choose, maintain systems, or provide professional advice. We may also disclose information when authorised or required by law, to protect safety or legal rights, or with your direction or consent.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Google receives analytics information only when Analytics is enabled. Meta receives advertising-event information only when Advertising is enabled. Products, internet services or accounts you ask us to configure may have their own privacy terms; we will ask you to review those terms where relevant rather than accepting optional data uses for you.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-overseas">
                <h2 id="privacy-overseas" class="text-2xl font-bold">8. Overseas processing and disclosure</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Some technology providers use global infrastructure. Cloudflare may process the security signals used by Turnstile in the United States, European Economic Area or other locations in its global network. If you enable Analytics or Advertising, information may be disclosed to or processed by Google or Meta in the United States and other countries where those providers and their service providers operate. Other hosting, communications, storage, security or payment suppliers may also process information outside Australia. Provider locations and subcontractors can change; you may ask us for the current information reasonably available about providers relevant to your information.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-retention">
                <h2 id="privacy-retention" class="text-2xl font-bold">9. Retention and security</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    We retain personal information only while it is reasonably needed for the purpose collected, customer support, security, a dispute, or legal and record-keeping obligations. Tax, invoice and transaction records may need to be retained for at least five years. When information is no longer needed and no law requires it to be kept, we take reasonable steps to delete it or de-identify it. Backup copies may remain inaccessible until they are overwritten through the normal backup cycle.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards appropriate to a small service business, including protected business accounts and access controls. No internet transmission or storage system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security. Tracking providers retain information under their own policies and our available account settings.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-access">
                <h2 id="privacy-access" class="text-2xl font-bold">10. Access, correction and deletion requests</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    You may ask what personal information we hold about you, request access or correction, or ask us to delete information that we no longer need to retain. Contact the Privacy Officer at <a href="mailto:privacy@nakedtech.au" class="font-bold text-accent-ink underline hover:text-ink">privacy@nakedtech.au</a> or call <a href="{{ site.phone.href }}" class="font-bold text-accent-ink underline hover:text-ink">{{ site.phone.display }}</a>. We may need to verify your identity. If a law permits or requires us to refuse or limit a request, we will explain that where required.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-complaints">
                <h2 id="privacy-complaints" class="text-2xl font-bold">11. Privacy questions and complaints</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    Send a privacy question or complaint to <a href="mailto:privacy@nakedtech.au" class="font-bold text-accent-ink underline hover:text-ink">privacy@nakedtech.au</a> with enough detail for us to investigate. We will acknowledge it and aim to provide a substantive response within 30 days. If you are not satisfied, and the Privacy Act applies to the matter, you may be able to complain to the <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-bold text-accent-ink underline hover:text-ink">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a>. The OAIC generally expects you to complain to the organisation first and allow it time to respond.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes">
                <h2 id="privacy-changes" class="text-2xl font-bold">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
                <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
                    We may update this policy when our information handling changes or the law requires it. The effective date at the top identifies the current version. Material changes apply from publication and do not authorise a new use of information where further notice or consent is required.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </article>
</div>
